1
00:00:49,125 --> 00:00:52,042
- <i>Jo, are you ready?</i>
- <i>Maybe, no. Um...</i>

2
00:00:52,083 --> 00:00:55,083
Yes, I'm all set.
Why don't you get something to eat?

3
00:00:57,083 --> 00:00:59,042
Jo, we're already late.

4
00:01:19,042 --> 00:01:21,250
Did you grab a bottle of wine?

5
00:01:41,083 --> 00:01:43,833
If we get hit, you could lose an eye.

6
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:49,333
Not today.

7
00:01:52,083 --> 00:01:53,708
How was your day?

8
00:01:54,875 --> 00:01:56,458
My day was fine.

9
00:02:07,708 --> 00:02:09,042
Thank you.

10
00:02:14,750 --> 00:02:16,875
- Michael, where's the wine?
- Sorry?

11
00:02:16,958 --> 00:02:18,750
- The wine?
- Shit! Hey!

12
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:27,042
No, wait, wait, wait.

13
00:02:27,125 --> 00:02:28,708
Hello.

14
00:02:31,875 --> 00:02:34,000
- You look nice, baby.
- Thanks.

15
00:02:37,583 --> 00:02:38,583
Come on.

16
00:02:51,625 --> 00:02:53,000
I love you.

17
00:02:54,625 --> 00:02:57,042
- Oh, you never bring Sarah.
- You didn't tell her?

18
00:02:57,083 --> 00:02:58,583
See you in an hour.

19
00:02:58,625 --> 00:03:01,042
- Should be finished by then.
- Oh, well, thank you for that.

20
00:03:01,708 --> 00:03:03,917
Barbara, hello. Thanks for having us.

21
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:06,458
- Come see me upstairs, all right?
- Will do.

22
00:03:07,042 --> 00:03:09,417
- How long were you two together?
- Three months.

23
00:03:09,500 --> 00:03:11,625
- Three months? Is it three months already?
- Mmm-hmm.

24
00:03:11,708 --> 00:03:12,875
Wow!

25
00:03:13,333 --> 00:03:16,000
About Munro, I think we should schedule
another reading for Monday.

26
00:03:16,083 --> 00:03:19,042
Okay. Let's just see how tomorrow goes.

27
00:03:19,125 --> 00:03:20,375
I bet you didn't even like Sarah, either,
did you?

28
00:03:20,417 --> 00:03:24,042
- No, I did! I said I did. - Hey! Yeah,
but I don't think that you meant it.

29
00:03:26,500 --> 00:03:27,542
- Thanks.
- You're welcome.

30
00:03:27,625 --> 00:03:29,208
Why is it so hard for me, Jo?

31
00:03:29,292 --> 00:03:32,708
It isn't. I mean, it can't be.
You haven't got to the hard bit yet.

32
00:03:32,750 --> 00:03:34,042
- What, it gets harder than this?
- Joanna!

33
00:03:34,083 --> 00:03:35,583
- Hello, hi.
- Hey, what's up?

34
00:03:35,667 --> 00:03:38,792
- So good to see you.
- Oh, thank you for having us.

35
00:03:38,875 --> 00:03:40,375
- Andy.
- Stuart.

36
00:03:43,083 --> 00:03:44,917
Michael's telling me
you're working on a new book.

37
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:47,333
- Michael always says that.
- Oh.

38
00:03:47,417 --> 00:03:48,917
- Well...
- Yeah.

39
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:50,625
He's probably right.

40
00:03:50,708 --> 00:03:51,917
- I just don't know it?
- Yeah.

41
00:03:55,750 --> 00:03:59,208
Well, I got to go talk to somebody.
Eat. I'll be here.

42
00:03:59,292 --> 00:04:01,000
<i>He hates me. He's gonna fire me.</i>
<i>I know it.</i>

43
00:04:01,083 --> 00:04:03,208
- <i>You say that every week.</i>
- <i>Yeah, well, it's true.</i>

44
00:04:03,292 --> 00:04:04,708
But it hasn't been in the last two years.

45
00:04:04,750 --> 00:04:06,625
Yeah, well, maybe he's just waiting
for the right time.

46
00:04:06,708 --> 00:04:09,167
Hey, do you want me to walk Lucy
while you guys are away?

47
00:04:09,250 --> 00:04:11,292
Oh, yeah. Yeah, that'd be great.

48
00:04:11,375 --> 00:04:13,042
Where is Michael, anyway?

49
00:04:14,833 --> 00:04:16,417
Oh, there he is.

50
00:04:17,250 --> 00:04:20,000
There he is, let's go. Joanna?

51
00:04:20,083 --> 00:04:23,958
Oh, yes. No, I'm gonna go
to the ladies' room. I'll catch up.

52
00:04:24,042 --> 00:04:25,125
Okay.

53
00:04:53,792 --> 00:04:55,333
I'm starving.

54
00:04:59,625 --> 00:05:02,500
Hey, where've you guys been?
I got totally ambushed by Stuart.

55
00:05:02,583 --> 00:05:06,292
The guy hasn't talked to me in two weeks,
he sees me with your wife and just lit up.

56
00:05:06,375 --> 00:05:07,708
- Hey.
- Hello.

57
00:05:07,750 --> 00:05:08,875
- Hey.
- Hi.

58
00:05:10,333 --> 00:05:11,875
Laura, this is my Joanna.

59
00:05:11,958 --> 00:05:13,000
- Hello. Nice to meet you.
- Hi.

60
00:05:13,083 --> 00:05:15,708
Joanna, this is Laura, she's the
new designer we've been working with.

61
00:05:15,792 --> 00:05:18,042
- Oh!
- Nice to finally meet you.

62
00:05:18,583 --> 00:05:20,208
So Michael tells me you're a writer.

63
00:05:20,250 --> 00:05:22,208
- Yeah, I am.
- I've been meaning to order your book.

64
00:05:23,208 --> 00:05:24,375
Oh, that's nice.

65
00:05:24,417 --> 00:05:27,833
Oh, look, look. Oh, my God, Neal,
he's trying with Cynthia again.

66
00:05:27,917 --> 00:05:30,042
- She's not gonna go for him.
- I know, he just won't learn.

67
00:05:30,083 --> 00:05:32,208
Why not? He's a good-looking guy.

68
00:05:32,250 --> 00:05:34,250
- Oh!
- Then why'd you turn him down?

69
00:05:34,333 --> 00:05:35,708
Oh, speak of the devil.

70
00:05:35,750 --> 00:05:36,750
- Hey, guys.
- Hey, Neal.

71
00:05:36,833 --> 00:05:38,083
No luck with Cynthia?

72
00:05:38,167 --> 00:05:40,083
- Oh, Joanna, hey. It's been forever.
- Hello!

73
00:05:40,125 --> 00:05:41,667
- No luck?
- What?

74
00:05:42,250 --> 00:05:44,167
You didn't really go to the yoga with her,
did you?

75
00:05:44,250 --> 00:05:46,292
She told you that?

76
00:05:46,375 --> 00:05:49,250
- She told me about that.
- Still trying with Cynthia, huh?

77
00:05:49,333 --> 00:05:51,125
What, getting jealous?

78
00:05:52,333 --> 00:05:56,000
- So, what's Laura's story?
- Stuart recruited her.

79
00:05:56,875 --> 00:05:58,583
She seems to be good.

80
00:05:59,625 --> 00:06:02,375
She's working the Munro project with us.

81
00:06:05,458 --> 00:06:07,125
Of course she is.

82
00:06:11,625 --> 00:06:14,708
- Do you mind getting me some more wine?
- Mmm-hmm.

83
00:06:22,833 --> 00:06:25,792
How mysterious...

84
00:06:25,875 --> 00:06:27,833
More of a necessary...

85
00:06:28,917 --> 00:06:30,542
That's not funny.

86
00:06:38,917 --> 00:06:40,083
- There you go.
- Hi.

87
00:06:40,167 --> 00:06:42,833
- Hey. You want a drink?
- Yeah. White wine, please.

88
00:06:42,917 --> 00:06:44,000
Sure.

89
00:06:46,750 --> 00:06:48,583
Can I get another one?

90
00:06:49,667 --> 00:06:52,583
<i>Is she going to Philly</i>
<i>with you guys tomorrow?</i>

91
00:06:52,667 --> 00:06:54,083
<i>Yeah.</i>

92
00:06:55,208 --> 00:06:56,917
And she was in LA with Michael last month?

93
00:07:07,042 --> 00:07:08,083
Hey!

94
00:07:12,250 --> 00:07:13,542
Have you been smoking?

95
00:07:15,375 --> 00:07:17,292
Are you really gonna attempt
to give me grief about that?

96
00:07:20,125 --> 00:07:21,167
What's wrong?

97
00:07:22,583 --> 00:07:23,833
Nothing.

98
00:07:27,875 --> 00:07:30,000
Have I done something wrong?

99
00:08:34,625 --> 00:08:36,125
She's pretty.

100
00:08:36,208 --> 00:08:37,250
Who?

101
00:08:38,583 --> 00:08:40,292
You never mentioned that.

102
00:08:40,375 --> 00:08:42,125
- Laura?
- Yeah, Laura.

103
00:08:43,417 --> 00:08:45,417
I think you described her as "whatever."

104
00:08:46,125 --> 00:08:48,500
- I don't remember.
- I bet.

105
00:08:54,417 --> 00:08:56,583
You didn't tell me
that she was in LA with you.

106
00:08:56,667 --> 00:08:59,167
She wasn't in LA with me.
We were just there at the same time.

107
00:08:59,250 --> 00:09:00,875
Michael, face me.

108
00:09:01,750 --> 00:09:03,667
You didn't tell me anything about her
before tonight,

109
00:09:03,750 --> 00:09:05,208
but then, I think you know that.

110
00:09:05,750 --> 00:09:07,958
What's that supposed to mean?

111
00:09:08,833 --> 00:09:11,542
What did you think would happen tonight?

112
00:09:11,625 --> 00:09:14,708
I mean, seriously.
Did you think I just wouldn't notice?

113
00:09:14,792 --> 00:09:17,250
Why would I think anything
about you noticing her?

114
00:09:17,292 --> 00:09:19,042
You are a terrible liar.

115
00:09:19,375 --> 00:09:20,875
Maybe because I don't lie.

116
00:09:20,958 --> 00:09:23,417
She likes you, and you like her.

117
00:09:23,458 --> 00:09:26,250
And of course
you don't want to talk to me about it.

118
00:09:26,333 --> 00:09:29,042
- Where does this come from?
- My eyes, Michael.

119
00:09:29,125 --> 00:09:31,417
She was the only one
you talked to all night.

120
00:09:31,500 --> 00:09:33,542
How many glasses of wine
did you have tonight, Jo?

121
00:09:33,583 --> 00:09:36,250
Two, and too few sips.
Is that really your response?

122
00:09:36,333 --> 00:09:39,875
- You had more than that.
- What are you, the drink patrol?

123
00:09:40,458 --> 00:09:43,417
You know that moment when we go out
and I ask you not to have another?

124
00:09:43,500 --> 00:09:46,042
And you ask me why? Well, this is why.

125
00:09:46,125 --> 00:09:47,250
You're kidding, right?

126
00:09:47,625 --> 00:09:49,375
Because it makes you like this, baby.

127
00:09:51,250 --> 00:09:55,042
Michael, without the wine,
you'd be in a much shittier place.

128
00:09:55,458 --> 00:09:58,542
Eleven hours a day,
five, sometimes six days a week.

129
00:09:58,625 --> 00:10:03,083
What, that's 60 hours a week with her
for three months now?

130
00:10:03,167 --> 00:10:04,542
What is it you think that I've done?

131
00:10:05,750 --> 00:10:07,542
Check my phone, Jo.

132
00:10:08,250 --> 00:10:12,083
- Check e-mail, check receipts. Go on.
- Oh, not everyone gets caught, Michael.

133
00:10:15,250 --> 00:10:19,250
- Has she told you she's attracted to you?
- I don't know. Maybe, Joanna.

134
00:10:20,167 --> 00:10:22,542
You know,
I don't let the conversation go there.

135
00:10:22,583 --> 00:10:24,083
But it's tried to, hasn't it?

136
00:10:24,500 --> 00:10:26,000
I bet it tried to when
you were in LA together.

137
00:10:27,458 --> 00:10:30,708
You have hours that I don't know about
with the people that you work with!

138
00:10:30,750 --> 00:10:34,375
You go away, doing your articles.

139
00:10:35,250 --> 00:10:36,708
All the time.

140
00:10:38,500 --> 00:10:41,083
And have I ever given you
a reason to stand here

141
00:10:41,167 --> 00:10:43,250
feeling the way that I am right now?

142
00:10:44,042 --> 00:10:47,750
I looked through a window tonight and I
saw something that I didn't need to see.

143
00:10:47,833 --> 00:10:50,417
You couldn't have just watched yourself
and spared me this?

144
00:10:50,500 --> 00:10:52,208
- What the fuck are you doing?
- Trying to charge the phone.

145
00:10:52,292 --> 00:10:53,917
Why do you always have to use this plug?

146
00:10:54,000 --> 00:10:57,292
Why'd you build a Berlin Wall
of frigging magazines?

147
00:10:59,583 --> 00:11:04,042
I haven't done anything wrong.
And you're trying to pick a fight.

148
00:11:05,958 --> 00:11:07,375
I spare you.

149
00:11:13,125 --> 00:11:14,375
I would.

150
00:11:19,083 --> 00:11:20,542
What's that supposed to mean?

151
00:11:23,167 --> 00:11:24,958
What's that supposed to mean?

152
00:11:27,333 --> 00:11:29,375
Is she going to Philadelphia
with you and Andy tomorrow?

153
00:11:29,417 --> 00:11:30,625
- Uh-huh.
- Mmm-hmm.

154
00:11:30,875 --> 00:11:32,708
Yeah, she's been working
on the Munro property with us.

155
00:11:34,625 --> 00:11:36,583
What? What is that look?

156
00:11:37,958 --> 00:11:39,417
That look's sad, Michael.

157
00:11:40,083 --> 00:11:44,042
There's nothing going on, Jo.
Laura's just someone I work with.

158
00:11:45,750 --> 00:11:48,500
It's not that I'm blaming you
for being attracted to her. She's

159
00:11:49,542 --> 00:11:50,875
attractive.

160
00:11:52,208 --> 00:11:53,167
And

161
00:11:54,417 --> 00:11:56,708
it's natural to crave a newness.

162
00:12:04,583 --> 00:12:06,958
Then what are you blaming me for?

163
00:12:07,542 --> 00:12:10,083
For going out of your way not to admit it.

164
00:12:12,500 --> 00:12:14,292
I thought I just did.

165
00:12:18,167 --> 00:12:20,667
Don't do that face, Jo...

166
00:12:27,250 --> 00:12:29,083
You know what I meant.

167
00:12:31,250 --> 00:12:34,125
You corner me and you order me
to admit something

168
00:12:34,208 --> 00:12:36,583
and then you pounce on me
the second I cave.

169
00:12:36,625 --> 00:12:40,375
And now you're gonna sleep on the couch?
Fucking fantastic!

170
00:12:42,542 --> 00:12:44,833
I didn't do anything wrong, Jo.

171
00:13:13,958 --> 00:13:15,292
I'm sorry.

172
00:13:17,667 --> 00:13:18,917
What for?

173
00:13:20,125 --> 00:13:21,875
I'm not sure. But...

174
00:13:22,583 --> 00:13:23,875
I love you.

175
00:13:24,958 --> 00:13:26,375
Come to bed.

176
00:13:27,250 --> 00:13:28,875
I don't want to.

177
00:13:33,042 --> 00:13:34,792
Come to the kitchen.

178
00:13:35,333 --> 00:13:37,375
Food isn't gonna fix this.

179
00:13:37,417 --> 00:13:39,958
Say that on a full stomach. Come on.

180
00:13:41,958 --> 00:13:44,250
- We got any tomatoes?
- No.

181
00:14:06,500 --> 00:14:07,833
How was your day?

182
00:14:07,917 --> 00:14:10,542
Mostly uneventful. Oh, but...

183
00:14:12,750 --> 00:14:15,250
- What?
- Nothing. I just remembered I'm mad at you.

184
00:14:15,333 --> 00:14:16,750
I hate it when that happens.

185
00:14:19,750 --> 00:14:21,042
Danny proposed.

186
00:14:21,125 --> 00:14:22,792
- Really?
- Yeah.

187
00:14:22,875 --> 00:14:25,125
- What'd Pia say?
- What do you think she said? "Yes."

188
00:14:25,208 --> 00:14:26,667
Was she surprised at all?

189
00:14:26,750 --> 00:14:28,875
She thought that he was gonna tell her
he was moving out.

190
00:14:40,000 --> 00:14:43,333
- My mom called, and...
- Yeah, I know. I spoke to her.

191
00:14:44,000 --> 00:14:46,125
Second week of December.
I've already said yes.

192
00:14:48,833 --> 00:14:51,333
- Can we go via London?
- Yeah. Sure.

193
00:14:54,500 --> 00:14:55,583
What time's your train?

194
00:14:56,500 --> 00:14:57,500
8:00.

195
00:14:57,583 --> 00:15:01,083
- You shouldn't be up this late.
- I'll sleep on the train.

196
00:15:01,167 --> 00:15:04,083
- It's an hour's ride.
- I'll sleep in the meeting.

197
00:15:05,792 --> 00:15:10,333
- What are you doing tomorrow, or today?
- I've gotta finish up the accessories piece.

198
00:15:10,417 --> 00:15:12,667
- Yeah? The pearls?
- Yeah.

199
00:15:12,750 --> 00:15:14,833
I've gotta dig up another 100 words.

200
00:15:14,917 --> 00:15:20,083
It's good. And then you'll be able to work
on the book without me here to distract you.

201
00:15:25,000 --> 00:15:26,667
Joanna, I'm sorry.

202
00:15:27,083 --> 00:15:31,500
I would have said something about her if
I thought that there was something to say.

203
00:15:33,417 --> 00:15:35,917
Michael, did something happen in LA?

204
00:15:36,250 --> 00:15:37,250
No.

205
00:15:37,958 --> 00:15:40,417
- You swear?
- I swear.

206
00:15:41,583 --> 00:15:42,625
No.

207
00:15:46,542 --> 00:15:48,000
Eggs are good.

208
00:15:50,250 --> 00:15:51,292
Yep.

209
00:16:02,208 --> 00:16:04,042
That the orange juice?

210
00:16:04,542 --> 00:16:07,125
Come on, what kind of caf  is this?

211
00:16:16,417 --> 00:16:19,000
Do you think we got married too soon?

212
00:16:22,583 --> 00:16:26,125
What? Why can't you
let yourself consider that?

213
00:16:28,667 --> 00:16:30,625
Because I don't have to.

214
00:16:32,167 --> 00:16:36,292
I don't think we got married too soon
because we married after four years.

215
00:16:36,375 --> 00:16:38,542
Yeah, but we broke up in the middle.

216
00:16:39,500 --> 00:16:41,417
And anyway,
it's not about the amount of time,

217
00:16:41,500 --> 00:16:44,917
it's about the "when" of time,
and our "when" included college.

218
00:16:45,000 --> 00:16:46,250
You know?

219
00:16:47,333 --> 00:16:50,042
It was before we were even us, you know?

220
00:16:52,625 --> 00:16:55,583
I mean, do you think
it's even the same between us?

221
00:16:57,708 --> 00:16:59,458
I think it's better.

222
00:17:03,583 --> 00:17:05,417
Can you hear yourself right now?

223
00:17:08,292 --> 00:17:09,375
What?

224
00:17:10,458 --> 00:17:15,125
Just because I disagree with you
means I'm not aware of what I'm saying?

225
00:17:15,208 --> 00:17:18,250
- You can't really think that.
- I do think that.

226
00:17:19,000 --> 00:17:20,042
How?

227
00:17:20,417 --> 00:17:23,708
Sunday night. The last two weekends.

228
00:17:23,792 --> 00:17:26,500
Breakfast yesterday. Dinner last night.

229
00:17:26,875 --> 00:17:29,167
There's no bullshit between us.

230
00:17:31,125 --> 00:17:34,083
With the possible exception of this evening.

231
00:17:38,417 --> 00:17:41,042
Come here, Joey. I'm cold.

232
00:18:46,583 --> 00:18:49,208
- Pack your running shoes?
- No.

233
00:18:50,583 --> 00:18:51,917
Thank you.

234
00:19:14,667 --> 00:19:16,333
You gonna try and get some writing done?

235
00:19:16,417 --> 00:19:18,875
- "Try" is a big word.
- No, it's not.

236
00:19:23,375 --> 00:19:25,042
I really gotta go.

237
00:19:25,875 --> 00:19:28,333
- See you later.
- Bye.

238
00:20:35,458 --> 00:20:37,333
Hello. Coffee.

239
00:20:53,708 --> 00:20:55,042
Joanna!

240
00:20:59,750 --> 00:21:02,250
Alex, what are you...
What are you doing here?

241
00:21:02,333 --> 00:21:03,375
I have some work here.

242
00:21:04,958 --> 00:21:06,042
I...

243
00:21:06,083 --> 00:21:08,583
I can't believe this!

244
00:21:08,667 --> 00:21:11,375
Yeah, it's been a while. How are you?

245
00:21:11,417 --> 00:21:14,292
Um... I'm fine. I just...

246
00:21:14,375 --> 00:21:16,417
I just can't believe you're here.
How did you know I'd be here?

247
00:21:16,500 --> 00:21:18,000
I keep tabs on you.

248
