In dream world, a mangy cat... What is that?

501
00:39:13,250 --> 00:39:14,667
- Whose phone is that?
- Sorry, it's me.

502
00:39:14,750 --> 00:39:18,625
It's... Michael's out of town, so excuse me.

503
00:39:27,458 --> 00:39:28,625
Hello. Hello.

504
00:39:28,708 --> 00:39:29,750
Hey.

505
00:39:30,583 --> 00:39:31,625
Where are you?

506
00:39:31,708 --> 00:39:35,583
Oh, I'm just grabbing a bite.
I just stepped out. How was your day?

507
00:39:37,208 --> 00:39:40,833
- Is that my phone or is that yours?
- It's gotta be yours. I hear you fine.

508
00:39:40,917 --> 00:39:41,917
<i>What?</i>

509
00:39:42,000 --> 00:39:43,875
I said I hear you fine.

510
00:39:44,583 --> 00:39:46,000
How was your day?

511
00:39:46,083 --> 00:39:48,042
<i>It was good. I got some work done.</i>

512
00:39:48,708 --> 00:39:50,375
<i>This isn't a very good connection.</i>

513
00:39:50,458 --> 00:39:52,333
No, it's not that good.

514
00:39:53,042 --> 00:39:54,417
Are you out?

515
00:39:54,917 --> 00:39:58,083
I'm in the men's room.
But we're still with the clients.

516
00:39:58,875 --> 00:40:02,000
<i>Okay. Why don't you give me</i>
<i>a call tomorrow morning?</i>

517
00:40:02,083 --> 00:40:03,167
Okay.

518
00:40:04,250 --> 00:40:05,375
I love you.

519
00:40:05,417 --> 00:40:07,208
- <i>I love you. Bye.</i>
- Bye.

520
00:40:24,292 --> 00:40:27,375
I love it when you come back
to the table and your food's there.

521
00:40:27,458 --> 00:40:30,542
- How long you been married?
- Three years.

522
00:40:30,917 --> 00:40:32,542
- You have any kids?
- No.

523
00:40:32,625 --> 00:40:35,042
- No. You?
- No.

524
00:40:35,083 --> 00:40:40,208
I never wanted any. In fact, that's
why my first wife and I broke up.

525
00:40:40,875 --> 00:40:42,625
That didn't come up before you got married?

526
00:40:42,708 --> 00:40:45,875
Well, yes, of course it did.
But I think she thought that

527
00:40:45,917 --> 00:40:49,667
I would change after we got married.
But people don't change.

528
00:40:50,792 --> 00:40:54,042
I mean, at most, your weight fluctuates
and you start dressing differently.

529
00:41:04,875 --> 00:41:07,458
<i>I realize, for a host of reasons, I...</i>

530
00:41:08,875 --> 00:41:12,750
I probably shouldn't be going here,
but I'm going to.

531
00:41:14,875 --> 00:41:18,375
That night in LA when
we all went to that bar,

532
00:41:18,458 --> 00:41:22,667
we sat on those low couches
and Jeff wanted to sit next to us

533
00:41:22,750 --> 00:41:25,000
so you had to move over.

534
00:41:26,875 --> 00:41:28,750
Your hand sort of

535
00:41:30,417 --> 00:41:32,250
rested against my leg.

536
00:41:34,250 --> 00:41:36,042
Was that on purpose?

537
00:41:41,750 --> 00:41:44,125
I had to be careful
not to really let it rest there.

538
00:41:47,583 --> 00:41:49,250
In case you moved.

539
00:41:50,083 --> 00:41:51,583
I didn't move.

540
00:41:52,333 --> 00:41:53,917
I wouldn't have.

541
00:42:15,875 --> 00:42:17,250
I'm married.

542
00:42:17,583 --> 00:42:18,792
I know.

543
00:42:21,708 --> 00:42:23,333
Still felt nice.

544
00:42:28,625 --> 00:42:31,167
Oh, that's so embarrassing.
Thank you, thanks.

545
00:42:31,250 --> 00:42:32,833
No, no, that's good.

546
00:42:32,917 --> 00:42:35,000
- Usually she's doing it better, but...
- No, the point...

547
00:42:35,083 --> 00:42:36,875
The point was that I love Italy.

548
00:42:36,958 --> 00:42:38,500
I love it there, I love it there.

549
00:42:38,583 --> 00:42:41,958
We have a place,
we go there about one month a year.

550
00:42:42,458 --> 00:42:44,125
It's so wonderful. Seriously.

551
00:42:44,208 --> 00:42:46,042
Wait, this is who you went to Italy with?

552
00:42:46,083 --> 00:42:47,083
When?

553
00:42:47,167 --> 00:42:49,417
When I got to Paris early
and your little cousin

554
00:42:49,500 --> 00:42:52,250
was staying in the apartment
until you got back, and you were away

555
00:42:52,333 --> 00:42:55,833
- with Patrick and his friends.
- Yeah, yeah. Exactly. This is them.

556
00:42:55,958 --> 00:42:58,917
Ah! No, it's so weird,
I knew you seemed familiar.

557
00:42:59,000 --> 00:43:00,458
Yeah, well...

558
00:43:00,792 --> 00:43:02,125
How funny.

559
00:43:07,042 --> 00:43:08,208
<i>What if you were married?</i>

560
00:43:10,750 --> 00:43:13,833
Well, hypotheticals
don't do much for me, but...

561
00:43:16,083 --> 00:43:18,167
Probably nothing different.

562
00:43:22,958 --> 00:43:24,458
Are you happy?

563
00:43:24,792 --> 00:43:25,875
With what?

564
00:43:27,417 --> 00:43:29,125
With your marriage.

565
00:43:29,458 --> 00:43:30,542
Yeah.

566
00:43:32,708 --> 00:43:33,792
Very.

567
00:43:36,958 --> 00:43:39,667
You can be happy and still be tempted.

568
00:43:39,750 --> 00:43:40,917
I know.

569
00:43:43,042 --> 00:43:45,042
I'm just surprised you do.

570
00:43:48,750 --> 00:43:52,542
Have you ever been with someone else
since you've been married?

571
00:43:52,583 --> 00:43:53,625
No.

572
00:43:54,583 --> 00:43:56,458
Have you wanted to be?

573
00:44:00,417 --> 00:44:01,875
What happens?

574
00:44:03,667 --> 00:44:05,667
I think of Joanna.

575
00:44:09,042 --> 00:44:11,167
Do you regret not doing it?

576
00:44:14,708 --> 00:44:16,875
I'd regret it more if I did.

577
00:44:29,250 --> 00:44:31,333
You ever cheated on anyone?

578
00:44:31,792 --> 00:44:33,125
"Cheated"?

579
00:44:33,917 --> 00:44:35,208
Have you?

580
00:44:36,375 --> 00:44:37,375
No.

581
00:44:39,250 --> 00:44:43,625
Not necessarily out of principle.
I just... I never wanted to.

582
00:44:48,583 --> 00:44:51,167
Alex, I know you want one.

583
00:44:51,250 --> 00:44:52,458
I need one, yeah.

584
00:44:54,583 --> 00:44:55,833
And I know you want one.

585
00:44:55,917 --> 00:44:58,417
No, no, no. She wants to keep me company.

586
00:44:58,792 --> 00:45:00,458
I do. I do.

587
00:45:00,542 --> 00:45:02,125
- You do?
- I do.

588
00:45:02,583 --> 00:45:05,250
Okay, so have a good night...

589
00:45:05,333 --> 00:45:07,333
It's a trap. I know it.

590
00:45:08,917 --> 00:45:10,625
He'll never change.

591
00:45:12,792 --> 00:45:14,708
When was the last time you saw Alex?

592
00:45:15,792 --> 00:45:17,542
Uh, two years ago.

593
00:45:17,625 --> 00:45:18,875
So you don't know Helen?

594
00:45:20,750 --> 00:45:21,792
Helen?

595
00:45:21,875 --> 00:45:24,000
Alex's girlfriend, from Paris.

596
00:45:27,625 --> 00:45:29,625
Well, we don't really
do... You know, we're...

597
00:45:29,708 --> 00:45:33,708
We're not very good
at keeping in touch with the dailies.

598
00:45:33,792 --> 00:45:36,458
- You know, we talk when we talk.
- Mmm-hmm.

599
00:45:36,542 --> 00:45:41,250
She's nice. I don't think he's gonna
settle down with her anytime soon but...

600
00:45:41,750 --> 00:45:45,542
I don't know that Alex
will ever settle down with anyone.

601
00:45:45,583 --> 00:45:47,958
He seems more whole on his own.

602
00:45:50,042 --> 00:45:51,792
So where is your husband?

603
00:45:51,875 --> 00:45:54,583
He's in Philadelphia on a business trip.

604
00:45:56,750 --> 00:45:58,208
What's he do?

605
00:45:58,292 --> 00:45:59,958
Commercial real estate development.

606
00:46:00,042 --> 00:46:03,792
But I don't think that that's the question
you wanted to ask.

607
00:46:03,875 --> 00:46:05,333
No. It wasn't.

608
00:46:05,958 --> 00:46:07,208
Go ahead.

609
00:46:07,583 --> 00:46:09,792
I usually tend to go too far.

610
00:46:10,792 --> 00:46:12,375
Okay, warning heard.

611
00:46:12,458 --> 00:46:14,583
Does your husband know Alex?

612
00:46:18,250 --> 00:46:19,250
No.

613
00:46:20,083 --> 00:46:21,333
Does he know of him?

614
00:46:21,417 --> 00:46:22,417
No.

615
00:46:23,083 --> 00:46:26,833
- Have I gone too far?
- Yeah, maybe. But it's fine.

616
00:46:28,125 --> 00:46:29,625
Why haven't you told him?

617
00:46:32,917 --> 00:46:36,875
I think, once you know something like that,
you can't unlearn it.

618
00:46:38,542 --> 00:46:40,667
So it is a "something like that."

619
00:46:42,917 --> 00:46:44,792
- Are you faithful?
- Yes.

620
00:46:47,583 --> 00:46:50,500
<i>Would he forgive you</i>
<i>if you weren't?</i>

621
00:46:50,583 --> 00:46:53,375
<i>He's always said that he wouldn't.</i>

622
00:46:53,875 --> 00:46:55,958
<i>Does that stop you?</i>

623
00:46:57,583 --> 00:46:59,083
Yeah, probably.

624
00:47:00,958 --> 00:47:02,417
How long were you and Alex together?

625
00:47:03,375 --> 00:47:06,667
We were never really together, you know.
We were more kind of...

626
00:47:06,750 --> 00:47:08,333
We were more on-and-off.

627
00:47:10,417 --> 00:47:13,542
You think you'll tell your husband
about tonight?

628
00:47:14,250 --> 00:47:17,042
I don't know. Tonight's not finished yet.

629
00:47:17,417 --> 00:47:18,667
Mmm.

630
00:47:35,917 --> 00:47:38,292
You remember the last time
we were here, we got in the wrong car?

631
00:47:38,375 --> 00:47:39,542
- Yeah.
- When was that?

632
00:47:39,583 --> 00:47:40,792
How far did we go
before we remembered?

633
00:47:40,875 --> 00:47:42,333
- When was that?
- About 10 blocks.

634
00:47:42,417 --> 00:47:44,833
Oh, my God, you guys, come on.
Why don't you just drive with us?

635
00:47:44,917 --> 00:47:46,750
- Yeah, come on.
- Oh, shit! Lucy.

636
00:47:46,833 --> 00:47:50,667
- Who?
- Our friend's dog. I said I'd walk her.

637
00:47:50,750 --> 00:47:53,250
- Where is she?
- She's at our friend's apartment.

638
00:47:54,583 --> 00:47:56,708
Are you just saying that
to get out of going to the party?

639
00:47:56,750 --> 00:47:58,958
- No, it's a very good excuse.
- No, no, I'm not. I swear.

640
00:48:01,417 --> 00:48:03,708
When were you last in New York?

641
00:48:04,750 --> 00:48:06,958
About nine months ago.

642
00:48:07,625 --> 00:48:10,042
Well, why didn't you get in touch?

643
00:48:11,792 --> 00:48:13,542
I wasn't alone.

644
00:48:15,125 --> 00:48:16,167
Oh.

645
00:48:56,417 --> 00:48:58,375
I can't get the key out.

646
00:49:33,792 --> 00:49:34,875
<i>Andy cooks?</i>

647
00:49:34,958 --> 00:49:39,125
No. I bought that for him last year.
I doubt he's ever used it.

648
00:49:40,417 --> 00:49:41,958
I do, though, when we're over.

649
00:49:42,042 --> 00:49:44,250
So why aren't you writing?

650
00:49:44,917 --> 00:49:46,542
I am writing.

651
00:49:46,625 --> 00:49:47,917
No. Why aren't you writing?

652
00:49:48,000 --> 00:49:50,292
- You mean...
- Your book, Joanna.

653
00:49:53,208 --> 00:49:57,167
My editor says that
I just need to get over my doubts.

654
00:49:58,708 --> 00:50:00,042
What do you doubt?

655
00:50:00,917 --> 00:50:02,542
Everything, Alex.

656
00:50:04,875 --> 00:50:08,792
I go to write and every word, every thought,

657
00:50:08,875 --> 00:50:12,792
every choice that I make leads to another
and I doubt every single one I make.

658
00:50:12,875 --> 00:50:15,125
It wasn't like this last time.

659
00:50:15,250 --> 00:50:20,458
You live with your first book all your life.
It's sort of... It comes out on its own.

660
00:50:21,917 --> 00:50:26,417
After that, though, it's different.
You can suddenly write anything,

661
00:50:27,417 --> 00:50:29,750
and you second-guess everything.

662
00:50:30,167 --> 00:50:32,000
Doubts will kill your work.

663
00:50:32,083 --> 00:50:34,583
Will they? I don't know.

664
00:50:35,958 --> 00:50:37,958
What's the matter with doubt?

665
00:50:38,042 --> 00:50:41,833
I think the world could use
a little more doubt. So I doubt.

666
00:50:41,917 --> 00:50:44,750
- For the good of the world?
- Hmm. Exactly.

667
00:50:45,917 --> 00:50:47,375
No, thank you.

668
00:50:48,917 --> 00:50:51,208
The first book was good, Joanna.

669
00:50:56,375 --> 00:50:59,875
You know, I think you might've
just ruined this kitchen for me.

670
00:50:59,958 --> 00:51:01,000
How?

671
00:51:01,917 --> 00:51:03,417
By being in it.

672
00:51:06,083 --> 00:51:08,208
I come here all the time.
And now you've been here.

673
00:51:18,125 --> 00:51:19,417
Okay.

674
00:51:19,500 --> 00:51:23,375
So, remind me why it didn't work.

675
00:51:24,542 --> 00:51:25,667
Geography.

676
00:51:25,750 --> 00:51:27,542
People live between two cities.

677
00:51:27,583 --> 00:51:29,708
I don't. And neither do you.

678
00:51:30,917 --> 00:51:31,875
And timing.

679
00:51:32,375 --> 00:51:33,375
You were broken up.

680
00:51:33,458 --> 00:51:35,292
Temporarily.

681
00:51:35,750 --> 00:51:39,750
Technically, whatever-ly. You know, I...
We got back together.

682
00:51:39,833 --> 00:51:42,333
After we'd already been together
for a really long time.

683
00:51:43,417 --> 00:51:44,958
You came after.

684
00:51:45,125 --> 00:51:48,208
Oh! So you're with him
because he came first?

685
00:51:49,417 --> 00:51:51,500
He did. And I love him.

686
00:51:52,917 --> 00:51:56,625
And I love you, too.
And I love being able to tell you the truth.

687
00:51:56,708 --> 00:52:02,208
And I love faith and loyalty
and all that shit. Even now.

688
00:52:04,083 --> 00:52:05,333
And this?

689
00:52:07,208 --> 00:52:08,292
This?

690
00:52:10,542 --> 00:52:13,958
I don't know that this would be what it is
on its own.

691
00:52:14,625 --> 00:52:19,625
I mean, this is only what it is
because it's something that's between me,

692
00:52:19,708 --> 00:52:23,500
my marriage to Michael,
you and your set of things.

693
00:52:26,708 --> 00:52:29,083
Does Andy have anything to drink?

694
00:52:36,250 --> 00:52:39,042
- What are my things?
- Nothing I'm criticizing.

695
00:52:39,125 --> 00:52:43,292
I'm just...
I know that if we went for it, we'd lose it.

696
00:52:44,708 --> 00:52:47,667
I think it's still as hard as it is
because we never wore it out.

697
00:52:47,750 --> 00:52:51,042
You know, we were just getting to know that
we weren't right for each other and then...

698
00:52:51,083 --> 00:52:52,542
You didn't want it.

699
00:52:52,583 --> 00:52:54,500
- No.
- No?

700
00:52:55,333 --> 00:52:57,625
I came to Paris for two months!

701
00:52:58,083 --> 00:52:59,500
You do hold that against me.

702
00:52:59,583 --> 00:53:01,458
I don't hold anything against you.

703
00:53:01,542 --> 00:53:03,500
I was finishing a book.

704
00:53:04,417 --> 00:53:07,042
I was too tired to figure out
what you being there even meant.

705
00:53:07,125 --> 00:53:10,667
Well, it should have meant
that you wanted to spend some time with me.

706
00:53:12,042 --> 00:53:15,917
- Look... God, it doesn't matter.
- No, no, no. It matters to me.

707
00:53:16,542 --> 00:53:19,208
Because I'm the one who has to see you here.

708
00:53:19,250 --> 00:53:23,042
I'm the one who has to look around Andy's
to see these pictures of you in this life.

709
00:53:25,250 --> 00:53:26,333
What?

710
00:53:27,083 --> 00:53:28,875
I was what you needed to be sure of Michael?

711
00:53:30,958 --> 00:53:32,000
No.

712
00:53:32,958 --> 00:53:35,208
No, it doesn't work like that.

713
00:53:39,583 --> 00:53:41,375
I think... I think...

714
00:53:42,792 --> 00:53:46,333
Maybe I've never wanted this to change.

715
00:53:47,417 --> 00:53:48,708
Everything...

716
00:53:49,875 --> 00:53:53,667
Everything changes.
Everything changes but this still hasn't.

717
00:53:55,333 --> 00:53:57,625
Not for me. Hasn't lessened.

718
00:54:00,375 --> 00:54:03,125
I saw you this morning and...

719
00:54:07,208 --> 00:54:10,958
And in the middle of most nights
when I can't sleep,

720
00:54:12,583 --> 00:54:14,333
I still replay you.

721
00:54:41,583 --> 00:54:44,042
I'm gonna take her out for a walk.

722
00:55:34,542 --> 00:55:36,042
The keys, Alex.

723
00:55:37,083 --> 00:55:39,292
I thought you took them with you.

724
00:55:39,375 --> 00:55:40,792
No.

725
00:55:40,875 --> 00:55:42,083
Ah, man.

726
00:55:42,625 --> 00:55:45,167
- Did you leave them upstairs?
- Yeah.

727
00:55:45,625 --> 00:55:47,542
- Can we buzz someone?
- Uh...

728
00:55:47,833 --> 00:55:48,833
Um...

729
00:55:48,917 --> 00:55:51,167
We could call Caroline, but...

730
00:55:58,375 --> 00:55:59,458
Shit.

731
00:57:01,583 --> 00:57:05,208
Give me that. I'll give it
back to you tomorrow. Let's go.

732
00:57:37,583 --> 00:57:40,333
- You weren't lying about the dog.
- No!

733
00:57:41,708 --> 00:57:43,917
- Come with me. Let's find Fred.
- Okay.

734
00:57:48,875 --> 00:57:52,167
Her husband's best friend's dog.

735
00:57:59,750 --> 00:58:02,208
Is she the one Chris told me about?

736
00:58:02,625 --> 00:58:04,042
I don't know.

737
00:58:04,125 --> 00:58:07,958
At Phillip's wedding,
after you'd just broken off with Lauren.

738
00:58:09,042 --> 00:58:12,083
I asked him what the
hell was wrong with you.

739
00:58:14,250 --> 00:58:15,750
I liked Lauren.

740
00:58:16,417 --> 00:58:19,125
But I like this one much more.

741
00:58:21,250 --> 00:58:23,375
She's smart.

742
00:58:23,583 --> 00:58:25,208
- Yeah.
- And she's funny.

743
00:58:25,292 --> 00:58:27,167
- Yeah.
- She's gorgeous.

744
00:58:27,667 --> 00:58:28,875
I know.

745
00:58:29,875 --> 00:58:31,500
And she's honest.

746
00:58:31,750 --> 00:58:36,625
Well, I mean, besides the fact she's out
with you when her husband's out of town.

747
00:58:36,917 --> 00:58:38,250
But she's married.

748
00:58:39,708 --> 00:58:41,625
- I know.
- No, you don't.

749
00:58:41,708 --> 00:58:43,958
No, you've never been married.

750
00:58:44,042 --> 00:58:48,000
I mean, fuck the vows,
it's the years you can't undo.

751
00:58:48,958 --> 00:58:52,625
You'll never be able to take away
the years with her husband.

752
00:58:53,333 --> 00:58:55,208
And the moment you try,

753
00:58:56,417 --> 00:58:58,208
this would be gone.

754
00:58:59,458 --> 00:59:00,708
Trust me.

755
00:59:01,750 --> 00:59:03,417
That'll be a shame.

756
00:59:06,083 --> 00:59:09,917
I bet you've had less than
100 days together, am I right?

757
00:59:12,875 --> 00:59:14,333
It's the best.

758
00:59:16,917 --> 00:59:18,250
Be smart.

759
00:59:19,292 --> 00:59:20,917
Keep it as it is.

760
01:00:14,583 --> 01:00:15,792
I'm in.

761
01:00:16,792 --> 01:00:18,125
Your turn.

762
01:00:24,417 --> 01:00:25,458
Here.

763
01:00:29,042 --> 01:00:30,417
Oh, come on.

764
01:00:30,833 --> 01:00:34,375
I'm not going to be the only one in here
in my underwear.

765
01:01:32,792 --> 01:01:35,542
You look uncomfortable.

766
01:01:35,583 --> 01:01:37,167
I am uncomfortable.

767
01:01:39,250 --> 01:01:41,042
You don't hold much back, do you?

768
01:01:41,125 --> 01:01:44,500
We're here in our underwear.
I think it's a little late for that, no?

769
01:02:46,042 --> 01:02:47,875
Do you remember that first night?

770
01:02:49,000 --> 01:02:52,208
- Do you ever think about it?
- Of course I do.

771
01:02:53,875 --> 01:02:57,875
I didn't want to go home,
and you put me in a taxi.

772
01:03:00,292 --> 01:03:01,667
And do you remember that night

773
01:03:01,750 --> 01:03:04,042
when we met that photographer
you were interviewing?

774
01:03:04,125 --> 01:03:06,625
- And he was drunk!
- And he was drunk.

775
01:03:08,333 --> 01:03:11,500
And you danced in that top of yours
with no back.

776
01:03:14,208 --> 01:03:15,417
Come on.

777
01:04:20,208 --> 01:04:21,917
Let's go.

778
01:05:19,042 --> 01:05:21,500
<i>So have you ever been cheated on?</i>

779
01:05:24,917 --> 01:05:25,958
No.

780
01:05:30,667 --> 01:05:32,125
Well, I have.

781
01:05:35,875 --> 01:05:38,333
The worst part was how I found out.

782
01:05:42,375 --> 01:05:44,458
We shared a photo account.

783
01:05:44,542 --> 01:05:47,750
And I went on the website
to order some pictures,

784
01:05:48,042 --> 01:05:51,375
and I saw the album
she'd decided to share with him.

785
01:05:52,792 --> 01:05:56,333
I think they were together
for the weekend or something.

786
01:05:57,208 --> 01:05:59,000
I could have done without the visuals.

787
01:06:00,042 --> 01:06:03,250
There was this one of them laughing so hard.

788
01:06:07,500 --> 01:06:10,875
- What happened?
- We fought like animals.

789
01:06:10,958 --> 01:06:13,625
Like animals, for about a month.

790
01:06:13,708 --> 01:06:16,542
And, you know, I was angry.

791
01:06:17,042 --> 01:06:20,208
Maybe because I thought I had to be.

792
01:06:21,875 --> 01:06:24,000
Or maybe because I was sad.

793
01:06:24,875 --> 01:06:29,042
But he still wanted to be with me.
And I still wanted to be with him.

794
01:06:29,333 --> 01:06:30,958
So what happened?

795
01:06:31,958 --> 01:06:33,500
We stayed together.

796
01:06:35,708 --> 01:06:38,333
Had the best year of our relationship.

797
01:06:40,500 --> 01:06:41,750
And then?

798
01:06:45,875 --> 01:06:47,125
He died.

799
01:06:49,667 --> 01:06:51,000
I'm sorry.

800
01:07:10,000 --> 01:07:12,208
You want anything to drink?

801
01:07:12,292 --> 01:07:13,833
No, I'm fine.

802
01:07:35,875 --> 01:07:38,208
<i>Do you think</i>
<i>you still would have been with him?</i>

803
01:07:41,500 --> 01:07:42,583
Yeah.

804
01:07:44,000 --> 01:07:45,375
Definitely.

805
01:07:48,292 --> 01:07:51,625
And I think I'd still be
here, attracted to you.

806
01:08:21,875 --> 01:08:25,208
You'll never guess what I was
upset about this morning.

807
01:08:25,292 --> 01:08:28,375
Michael had a work thing last night
and we went

808
01:08:29,375 --> 01:08:33,667
and I accused him of being attracted
to this woman he's working with.

809
01:08:33,708 --> 01:08:35,542
- Was he?
- I think so.

810
01:08:37,458 --> 01:08:39,000
You think there's something going on?

811
01:08:39,875 --> 01:08:41,375
There could be.

812
01:08:42,167 --> 01:08:44,375
I think he'd want there to be.

813
01:08:46,375 --> 01:08:49,208
He's in Philadelphia with her right now.

814
01:08:49,292 --> 01:08:50,833
Are you worried?

815
01:08:52,542 --> 01:08:55,500
- I think I made too big a deal out of it.
- Why?

816
01:08:57,375 --> 01:08:59,667
It's 2:00 in the morning
and I'm here with you.

817
01:09:04,375 --> 01:09:05,375
It's funny how you can get up

818
01:09:05,458 --> 01:09:08,417
and have absolutely no idea
where the day will go.

819
01:09:08,500 --> 01:09:12,583
Eighty, 90, 1,000 go by

820
01:09:13,375 --> 01:09:16,750
without incident, and then all of a sudden,
"Hello."

821
01:09:17,708 --> 01:09:18,875
Hello.

822
01:09:21,000 --> 01:09:24,208
What if I hadn't come out
for coffee this morning?

823
01:09:24,625 --> 01:09:26,375
I would have called.

824
01:09:27,042 --> 01:09:29,000
If my number had changed?

825
01:09:30,667 --> 01:09:33,000
Then I would have come upstairs.

826
01:09:33,542 --> 01:09:34,583
What about Michael?

827
01:09:44,167 --> 01:09:46,375
Why did you stop e-mailing me?

828
01:09:52,375 --> 01:09:54,333
Because it wasn't enough.

829
01:09:58,625 --> 01:10:02,125
Do you know how often
I have to make a choice not to write?

830
01:10:03,208 --> 01:10:06,917
"Hello, Alex. How are you?
Where are you? What are you doing?

831
01:10:08,458 --> 01:10:11,542
"Do you want to meet me? Wherever.

832
01:10:13,167 --> 01:10:15,167
"This Friday, for dinner?

833
01:10:16,000 --> 01:10:17,708
"Just to catch up."

834
01:10:22,542 --> 01:10:25,958
You really touch me
whenever you feel like it, don't you?

835
01:10:26,042 --> 01:10:27,417
No, I don't.

836
01:10:28,792 --> 01:10:32,042
I touch you a fraction
of how often I feel like it.

837
01:10:34,542 --> 01:10:35,625
Why?

838
01:10:40,167 --> 01:10:41,875
Because I like you.

839
01:11:01,333 --> 01:11:02,917
I can't.

840
01:11:07,875 --> 01:11:11,500
I can't do any more and look him in the eye.

841
01:11:23,875 --> 01:11:28,167
You just told me he's away
with the woman you got upset about.

842
01:11:33,125 --> 01:11:35,333
Michael isn't doing anything.

843
01:11:51,292 --> 01:11:54,083
Do you know I've never told him about us?

844
01:11:55,125 --> 01:11:59,333
You know, even when I've felt the need
to confess something.

845
01:11:59,833 --> 01:12:01,333
Which is when?

846
01:12:02,708 --> 01:12:05,125
When we're drunk, or happy, or...

847
01:12:06,708 --> 01:12:09,708
Or after a fight. Or in the middle of one,
you know, when things slip out.

848
01:12:09,792 --> 01:12:11,333
This never does.

849
01:12:11,375 --> 01:12:13,375
Why? Would he be angry?

850
01:12:16,958 --> 01:12:18,958
He'd have no right to be.

851
01:12:19,958 --> 01:12:21,458
I gave you up.

852
01:12:35,000 --> 01:12:36,792
So what's Helen like?

853
01:12:53,208 --> 01:12:55,375
We have another couple hours.

854
01:12:56,167 --> 01:12:59,208
I don't want to spend them
talking about Helen.

855
01:13:00,792 --> 01:13:02,042
Come on.

856
01:13:05,833 --> 01:13:06,917
Jo.

857
01:13:10,708 --> 01:13:12,042
Come here.

858
01:16:01,875 --> 01:16:02,875
Jo.

859
01:16:08,708 --> 01:16:11,042
- What time is it?
- 6:30.

860
01:16:39,333 --> 01:16:40,542
Laura...

861
01:16:40,833 --> 01:16:43,792
Michael, I don't need us to talk about it.

862
01:16:46,708 --> 01:16:49,042
- Last night...
- Michael, please.

863
01:16:49,833 --> 01:16:51,292
Just... Don't.

864
01:16:57,042 --> 01:16:59,083
I didn't think that would happen.

865
01:17:01,667 --> 01:17:03,625
Not even the second time?

866
01:18:15,042 --> 01:18:17,833
Well, there's so much going on right now,
isn't there?

867
01:18:24,708 --> 01:18:27,542
What I wouldn't give to have tired of you.

868
01:18:35,042 --> 01:18:37,833
- Let me drop you off.
- No. I'd rather walk.

869
01:18:38,708 --> 01:18:40,333
- Sure?
- Yeah. It'll be good for her.

870
01:18:40,375 --> 01:18:42,208
It'll be good for me.

871
01:18:43,750 --> 01:18:46,708
Let's not do this in a
big way, okay? Please?

872
01:18:54,917 --> 01:18:55,917
See you.

873
01:21:10,042 --> 01:21:11,708
Hey, Andy, it's me.

874
01:21:13,792 --> 01:21:15,583
I need you to cover for me.

875
01:21:55,125 --> 01:21:57,083
- Hey.
- Hey.

876
01:21:57,167 --> 01:21:58,250
- You ready?
- Yeah.

877
01:21:58,333 --> 01:21:59,500
Where's Michael?

878
01:22:00,125 --> 01:22:01,458
He had to go back to New York.

879
01:22:03,042 --> 01:22:04,875
- Is everything okay?
- Yeah, yeah.

880
01:22:04,917 --> 01:22:08,708
He left me a voicemail.
I guess Stuart needed him to go back.

881
01:22:09,167 --> 01:22:10,167
Oh.

882
01:22:11,208 --> 01:22:13,458
- Okay.
- I'll see you out front.

883
01:24:03,917 --> 01:24:05,208
Joey.

884
01:24:10,750 --> 01:24:12,708
What are you doing back?

885
01:24:13,500 --> 01:24:15,375
What's Lucy doing here?

886
01:24:16,208 --> 01:24:17,917
We got locked out of Andy's.

887
01:24:18,417 --> 01:24:20,500
- Who?
- Me and Lucy.

888
01:24:22,125 --> 01:24:23,125
When?

889
01:24:25,375 --> 01:24:29,583
Um, last night, when I
went over to walk her.

890
01:24:30,708 --> 01:24:33,917
- Have you been crying, Joey?
- A little bit.

891
01:24:37,750 --> 01:24:39,542
What are you doing back?

892
01:24:41,792 --> 01:24:43,583
We finished up early.

893
01:24:44,958 --> 01:24:47,833
- I thought the presentation was today.
- No.

894
01:24:49,083 --> 01:24:51,083
No, we finished up early.

895
01:24:57,042 --> 01:24:58,833
I'm sorry about our fight.

896
01:25:02,208 --> 01:25:03,708
Yeah. So am I.

897
01:25:05,583 --> 01:25:07,833
- Let's not talk about it, okay?
- No.

898
01:25:11,083 --> 01:25:14,417
Let's have a great lunch and, you know,
let's walk,

899
01:25:15,542 --> 01:25:18,000
let's, you know, make a day of it.

900
01:25:19,250 --> 01:25:20,333
Okay.

901
01:25:23,167 --> 01:25:25,833
- Does she want to go out?
- Probably.

902
01:25:26,458 --> 01:25:27,750
I'll take her.

903
01:25:28,208 --> 01:25:29,417
Come on.

904
01:25:35,208 --> 01:25:36,167
Hey.

905
01:25:40,708 --> 01:25:42,000
You okay?

906
01:25:43,042 --> 01:25:44,167
Yeah.

907
01:25:56,042 --> 01:25:57,792
I love you.
